    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "The present study aimed to replicate previous findings on the positive association between connectedness to nature and body appreciation, using the BAS-2 in a U.S. community adult population. It also examined direct associations between nature exposure and body appreciation, hypothesizing positive links for both women and men. Furthermore, the study explored whether self-esteem mediates the relationship between nature-related variables and body appreciation, and investigated associations with broader body image variables like investment in physical appearance, perceived pressure from tripartite sources, and internalisation of appearance ideals.",
